{
  "anomaly_detected": false,
  "confidence": 0.72,
  "anomalies": [],
  "summary": "The KiCad netlist is internally consistent and implements every function the specification describes: 24V input with F1 fuse, D2 TVS clamp and a P-channel AON6407 (T3) high-side reverse-polarity switch; TPS62933 (U1) buck to +5V with the correct FB divider (R14 52k3/R15 10k -> ~4.98V), RT (R13), SS (C10) and BST (C12); AZ1117 (U2) to +3V3; two ADM3260 isolators (U3/U4) with isolated I2C pull-ups and VSEL dividers feeding the pH/EC EZO circuits; RTD on the non-isolated bus; three TMC2209 drivers with 110mOhm current-sense resistors, VREF dividers and a shared UART; and the IRLR2905 (T2) main-pump and AO3400A (T5) ATO-valve low-side switches with their flyback diodes. The apparent mismatches are not board anomalies: the spec's component table mis-attributes T3 (it actually serves as reverse-polarity protection while T5 switches the valve, and AON6407 is a P-channel part, not N-channel as the table states), and the firmware GPIO map, the unwired TF-Luna (PR1), the DNP BME280/BH1750 (PR5/PR6) and the absent DS18B20/one-wire net are all explicitly documented known limitations rather than deviations in the design files."
}

